<!--
  The words of the interface, in English.

  This dictionary is merged ON TOP of the French one, never instead of it. A key nobody
  translated therefore falls back to French, which reads — rather than to the key name,
  which does not.

  Two liberties were taken with the source, both deliberate. « Formulation » became
  « phrasing » rather than the false friend « formulation »: what the pilot types is the
  way they happen to say a thing, not a formula. And « mot d'éveil » became « wake word »,
  the term the speech-recognition world already uses — inventing a synonym would only make
  the setting harder to search for.
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

