  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.WhisperMissing">Whisper is not installed. Put whisper-cli.exe and at least one ggml-*.bin model in {0} — the Optimus installer can do it for you.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.WhisperTrimmed">Shorter window: about twice as fast, but the word error rate goes from 9.8% to 14.8%.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.WhisperOnDoubt">The fast engine keeps whatever it recognises cleanly — instant, as it is today. Whisper gets everything else: the rejections, but also the doubtful utterances, which is where most free speech actually lands. Reckon on about 900 ms in those cases, and nothing at all on commands it heard properly.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.WhisperAlways">Every utterance is transcribed, commands included. Measured: about 900 ms per command, and 9.8% of words wrong where the closed grammar returns 0.825 confidence — “turn on the lights” can come back as “turn on the light”. Fuzzy matching recovers some of it. Worth trying on your own voice before settling on it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.WhisperOff">Off. Optimus keeps to its closed grammar: anything that is not a known command is never transcribed, anywhere. The conversational layer is then out of reach by voice.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AiOff">Disabled. Optimus runs entirely offline: the catalogue and the grammar are enough, and nothing goes over the network.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AiLocal">The model runs on this machine. What you say does not leave it. It only steps in after the fast path fails, and can only name a command from the catalogue — never a key.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.AiRemote">Remote service: the utterances Optimus did not understand will be sent to it. Any key goes through the OPTIMUS_AI_KEY environment variable, never through a configuration file.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.NoRecognizer">Windows has no speech pack for “{0}” on this machine: Optimus will write and answer in this language, but will not be able to hear you. Add it under Settings &gt; Time &amp; language &gt; Language, ticking “Speech recognition” among the features.</sys:String>
